# SCSS Standards

## Critical Rules - NEVER Violate

### 1. NEVER Use Raw px Values

```scss
// ❌ NEVER do this
.component {
	font-size: 18px;
	padding: 24px;
	margin-bottom: 32px;
	gap: 16px;
}

// ✅ Use rem-calc() for fixed values
.component {
	border-radius: rem-calc(8);
	gap: rem-calc(16);
}

// ✅ Use fluid() for responsive values
.component {
	font-size: fluid(16, 18);
	padding: fluid(16, 24);
	margin-bottom: fluid(24, 32);
}
```

**Exceptions where px is allowed:**

- `1px` borders
- Box shadows
- Very small values (under 4px)

### 2. NEVER Use @media Directly

```scss
// ❌ NEVER do this
@media (min-width: 768px) {
}
@media (max-width: 768px) {
}
@media screen and (min-width: 992px) {
}

// ✅ ALWAYS use media queries up
@media (width >= $md) {
}
@media (width >= $lg) {
}
```

### 3. NEVER Use Desktop-First media queries

```scss
// ❌ NEVER do this
.component {
	font-size: fluid(24, 32);
	display: grid;
	grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);

	@media (width < $md) {
		font-size: fluid(16, 20);
		grid-template-columns: 1fr;
	}
}

// ✅ ALWAYS mobile-first
.component {
	font-size: fluid(16, 20);
	display: grid;
	grid-template-columns: 1fr;

	@media (width >= $lg) {
		font-size: fluid(24, 32);
		grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
	}
}
```

## The rem-calc() Function

Use for single pixel values that don't need responsive scaling.

```scss
// rem-calc(value) - converts px to rem
// Pass the value WITHOUT px unit

border-radius: rem-calc(8);
gap: rem-calc(16);
border-width: rem-calc(2);
padding: rem-calc(24);

// Multiple values
padding: rem-calc(16) rem-calc(24);
```

## The fluid() Function

Use for responsive values that scale between mobile and desktop.

### Basic Usage

```scss
// fluid(min-value, max-value)
// Values are unitless (px implied)
font-size: fluid(16, 24);
padding: fluid(20, 40);
margin-bottom: fluid(32, 64);
gap: fluid(16, 32);
```

### With Custom Breakpoints

```scss
// fluid(min-value, max-value, min-breakpoint, max-breakpoint)
// Use breakpoint NAMES not px values
font-size: fluid(16, 24, md, xl);
padding: fluid(20, 40, sm, xxl);
```

### Implementation (in partials/mixins/\_rem.scss)

```scss
@function fluid(
	$min-value,
	$max-value,
	$min-breakpoint: 'sm',
	$max-breakpoint: 'xxl'
) {
	// Returns clamp() with calculated values
	// @return clamp(min-rem, preferred, max-rem);
}
```

## Breakpoint System

### Available Breakpoints (Mobile-First ONLY)

```scss
// In partials/config/_maps.scss
$grid-breakpoints: (
	'xs': 0,
	'ph': 23.4375rem,
	// 375px
	'sm': 36rem,
	// 576px
	'md': 48rem,
	// 768px
	'lg': 62rem,
	// 992px
	'xl': 75rem,
	// 1200px
	'xxl': 87.5rem,
	// 1400px
	'xxxl': 100rem // 1600px
);
```

### Usage Pattern

```scss
.component {
	// Mobile styles (default)
	padding: fluid(16, 20);

	@media (width >= $sm) {
		// 576px and up
	}

	@media (width >= $md) {
		// 768px and up
		padding: fluid(20, 32);
	}

	@media (width >= $lg) {
		// 992px and up
		padding: fluid(32, 48);
	}

	@media (width >= $xl) {
		// 1200px and up
	}

	@media (width >= $xxl) {
		// 1400px and up
	}
}
```

## Naming Convention

### Class Names

```scss
// Use lowercase with hyphens
.hero-slider-section {
}
.header-nav-toggle {
}
.site-header {
}
.container-fluid {
}

// Section naming (full-width blocks)
.block-name-section {
}

// Inner wrappers (rare)
.inner-section {
}

// JS-controlled classes use 'js-' prefix
.js-active {
}
.js-popup-active {
}
```

### BEM (Optional)

```scss
// Block
.card {
}

// Element
.card__header {
}
.card__body {
}

// Modifier
.card--featured {
}
```

## File Organization

### SCSS Structure

```
src/sass/
├── partials/
│   ├── config/
│   │   ├── _colors.scss
│   │   ├── _maps.scss        # Breakpoints, spacings
│   │   ├── _typography.scss
│   │   └── _variables.scss
│   ├── mixins/
│   │   ├── _breakpoints.scss
│   │   ├── _rem.scss         # rem-calc(), fluid()
│   │   ├── _containers.scss
│   │   └── ...
│   ├── acf-blocks/
│   ├── components/
│   ├── helpers/
│   ├── templates/
│   └── utilities/
└── style.scss
```

### Import Order in style.scss

```scss
// 1. Mixins (utilities first - rem-calc needs to be first)
@import 'partials/mixins/rem';

// 2. Config
@import 'partials/config/maps';
@import 'partials/config/colors';
@import 'partials/config/typography';
@import 'partials/config/variables';

// 3. Rest of mixins
@import 'partials/mixins/breakpoints';
@import 'partials/mixins/placeholders';
// ... other mixins

// 4. Base styles
@import 'partials/reset';
@import 'partials/reboot';

// 5. JS Plugins (for easy overwrite)
@import 'partials/js-plugins/swiper';

// 6. Components
@import 'partials/components/header';

// 7. ACF Blocks
@import 'partials/acf-blocks/hero-slider';

// 8. Templates
@import 'partials/templates/index';

// 9. Helpers & Utilities (last)
@import 'partials/helpers/buttons';
@import 'partials/utilities/images';
```

## Indentation & Formatting

### Use Tabs (Not Spaces)

```scss
// ✅ Correct - tabs for indentation
.component {
	display: flex;
	gap: rem-calc(16);

	@media (width >= $md) {
		gap: fluid(16, 32);
	}
}
```

## CSS Variables Pattern

```scss
// Global variables
:root {
	--header-height: #{rem-calc(65)};
	--container-padding-x: #{fluid(20, 40)};
}

// Use in components
.component {
	padding-inline: var(--container-padding-x);
	margin-top: var(--header-height);
}
```

## Common Patterns

### Grid Layout

```scss
.grid {
	display: grid;
	gap: fluid(16, 32);
	grid-template-columns: 1fr;

	@media (width >= $md) {
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
	}

	@media (width >= $lg) {
		grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
	}
}
```

### Flexbox Layout

```scss
.flex-container {
	display: flex;
	flex-direction: column;
	gap: fluid(12, 16);

	@media (width >= $md) {
		flex-direction: row;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: space-between;
	}
}
```

### Full-Height Section

```scss
.hero-section {
	block-size: calc(100svh - var(--header-height, rem-calc(65)));
	position: relative;
}
```

### Image Cover Block

```scss
.img-cover-block {
	position: absolute;
	inset: 0;
}

.img-cover {
	width: 100%;
	height: 100%;
	object-fit: cover;
}
```

## Nesting Rules

### Maximum 3 Levels

```scss
// ✅ Good - Clean and readable
.card {
	padding: fluid(16, 24);

	.card__title {
		font-size: fluid(18, 24);
	}
}

// ❌ Bad - Too deep
.card {
	.card__header {
		.card__title {
			.card__title-text {
				// Too deep!
			}
		}
	}
}
```

### Acceptable Deep Nesting

```scss
// Pseudo-classes and media queries don't count toward depth
.button {
	background: $color-primary;

	&:hover {
		background: darken($color-primary, 10%);
	}

	@media (width >= $md) {
		padding: fluid(16, 24);
	}
}
```

## Specificity Rules

### Keep It Low

```scss
// ✅ Good - Single class
.button {
}
.card__title {
}

// ❌ Avoid - High specificity
#header .navigation .menu-item {
}
div.card > p.text {
}
```

### Never Use !important

```scss
// ❌ Never
.component {
	color: red !important;
}

// ✅ Fix the specificity issue instead
```

## Accessibility

### Focus Styles

```scss
.button {
	&:focus-visible {
		outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
		outline-offset: 2px;
	}
}

// Never remove focus outlines without replacement
// ❌ Never
*:focus {
	outline: none;
}
```

### Reduced Motion

```scss
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
	*,
	*::before,
	*::after {
		animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;
		animation-iteration-count: 1 !important;
		transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
	}
}
```
